    "status": "present",
    "value": "Walk the seat pairs from left to right. For pair (2j, 2j+1), the person in seat 2j has a partner seats[2j] ^ 1. If the partner is not already in seat 2j+1, swap the partner into seat 2j+1 with whoever sits there, updating a where[] index of each person's seat. Each swap completes at least one couple and never breaks a completed one. This is optimal: viewing seat pairs as nodes and couples as edges, the graph splits into cycles, a cycle of c pairs needs exactly c-1 swaps, and the greedy uses exactly that."
  },
